 4 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 786f6bf..1f2b2ca 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -155,6 +155,10 @@ A gamepad is recommended ([Controls](#controls)). The game folder is never modif
 | **Ray tracing** | ✅ | BLAS / TLAS built on the GPU by the game's own XboxBvhBuilder; RDNA2 BVH node format; BVH intersection instructions emulated in shaders | GPU traversal = brute force reference; the game's builder output checked on the GPU |
 | **Upscaling** | ✅ | the game's AMD FSR 4 console DLL (`amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_xbox.dll`): context, the 29 pipelines in the console driver's own container (FSPX) translated, a frame's 20 passes recorded and run on the GPU | end-to-end with the real DLL: a 1280×720 → 1920×1080 frame on an RX 9070, the input's gradient in the output |
 
+With `XCL_DIRECT_DXIL=all`, set `XCL_DIRECT_PIXEL_MASK_PROJECTION=1` to try direct pixel
+translation that keeps the original wave ballots and extracts only a lane's bit at eligible uses.
+The option defaults to off. Its translated pixel shaders have a separate disk cache identity.
+
 Far-jump address calculations are resolved to fixed targets only when branches enter at the start of the calculation.
 An entry partway through it keeps the jump indirect and subject to the recompiler's existing indirect-branch limits.
 
diff --git a/crates/xcl/src/gpu/dxil/kernel.rs b/crates/xcl/src/gpu/dxil/kernel.rs
index 04adb0e..b4cf58a 100644
--- a/crates/xcl/src/gpu/dxil/kernel.rs
+++ b/crates/xcl/src/gpu/dxil/kernel.rs
@@ -53,6 +53,13 @@ pub fn enabled_graphics() -> bool {
     std::env::var("XCL_DIRECT_DXIL").is_ok_and(|v| v == "all")
 }
 
+/// Opt in to exact own-bit projection at pixel mask consumers. The cache and
+/// translator must use the same policy throughout the process.
+pub(crate) fn project_pixel_masks() -> bool {
+    static ENABLED: std::sync::OnceLock<bool> = std::sync::OnceLock::new();
+    *ENABLED.get_or_init(|| std::env::var("XCL_DIRECT_PIXEL_MASK_PROJECTION").as_deref() == Ok("1"))
+}
+
